# What the project writes for itself, not what you write.

# Type stubs of your components. With DEBUG on, wireview writes one beside each
# module that defines components (hello/live.pyi) whenever Django starts --
# runserver, check, migrate -- so they would show as changed in every commit.
# Turn it off with WIREVIEW = {"AUTO_GENERATE_STUBS": False}. If you also keep
# stubs of your own, list the generated ones here instead of *.pyi.
*.pyi

# IDE metadata from `manage.py wireview_lsp`.
.wireview/

# The development database `migrate` makes.
db.sqlite3

# Python's bytecode cache.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# collectstatic's output, when STATIC_ROOT points here.
staticfiles/
